{"schema": 1, "provider": "codex", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "request_sha256": "1142b4954c3fe1dd57c40797772b39bc9a2f973583356f5590973e8d0401f159", "invocation_metadata": {"schema": 1, "image_id": "sha256:79462fb575e55c574c60e95256406443339fd0aebddbaddec572b8d1b632ae39", "executable_path": "/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/bin/codex.js", "executable_sha256": "61b0194f3bb6534439c8d26a3ed57d0805f84b884588b761795323eeb92fcf70", "known_configuration_path": "/home/codex/.codex/config.toml", "known_configuration_sha256": "c8597a1fbc447e945c45fc00126a131d9c3a824d2e6f96a57288de382363b87a", "other_effective_configuration": "unknown; trusted launcher/profile boundary", "response_schema_sha256": "374d4bb692012196f95c8105308100b0aeebe7a8fcc28fcb12010183313548a8", "response_schema_scope": "Prompt guidance and strict local validation only; no provider enforcement claim", "public_model_catalog_sha256": "fd219bd9f061278275f528939f82f54d2eb97df4b25c23b022adbe48813d920b", "runtime_model_catalog_sha256": "5f16461bf0477c6e522b6cdbb66d627a246e0da675721fe8cb8b35163cb736c9", "tool_surface_override": "direct; no shell, patch, search or experimental tools", "requested_reasoning_effort": "medium", "effective_remote_reasoning_effort": "not observed", "effective_features": {"disabled_features": ["apps", "plugins", "remote_plugin", "hooks", "daemon_auto_start", "shell_tool", "code_mode_host", "browser_use", "browser_use_external", "browser_use_full_cdp_access", "computer_use", "in_app_browser", "image_generation", "view_image", "multi_agent", "multi_agent_v2", "skill_search", "sleep_tool", "goals", "tool_suggest", "workspace_dependencies", "request_permissions_tool", "agent_message_board"], "unified_exec_observed": true, "shell_registration_control": "shell_tool=false; Codex 0.160.0 spec_plan.rs", "complete_configuration_isolation": false}}, "native_exit_code": 0, "usage_reported": {"input_tokens": 24269, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "cache_write_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 6477, "reasoning_output_tokens": 1034}, "native_reconnections": [], "result": {"schema": 1, "reason": "Se añade únicamente una batería nueva con fixtures integrados, carga absoluta y cobertura de los criterios originales. No se afirma ejecución ni resultado; programa y README sellados permanecen intactos.", "files": {"test_ledger_fold.py": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Standalone stdlib battery; fixture expectations come from the public contract.\"\"\"\nimport ast\nimport io\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport runpy\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest import mock\n\nPROGRAM = Path('/input/delivery/ledger_fold.py')\nLIMIT = 131072\nERROR = b'ledger-fold: invalid input\\n'\nEMPTY = {'balances': {}, 'total': 0, 'count': 0, 'zero_accounts': []}\nCASES = []\n\n\ndef encode(value):\n    return json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(',', ':')).encode('ascii')\n\n\ndef request(entries):\n    return encode({'entries': entries})\n\n\ndef entry(account, delta):\n    return {'account': account, 'delta': delta}\n\n\ndef result(balances, total, count, zero):\n    return {'balances': balances, 'total': total, 'count': count, 'zero_accounts': zero}\n\n\ndef valid(label, data, expected):\n    CASES.append((label, data, expected))\n\n\ndef invalid(label, data):\n    CASES.append((label, data, None))\n\n\ndef need(condition, code):\n    if not condition:\n        raise AssertionError(code)\n\n\ndef unique(pairs):\n    output = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in output:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate output key')\n        output[key] = value\n    return output\n\n\ndef finite(value):\n    raise ValueError('non-finite output')\n\n\n# C01, C02, C07-C10: explicit public examples and stream framing.\nvalid('empty stdin', b'', [])\nbase = request([])\nvalid('empty entries', base + b'\\n', [EMPTY])\nvalid('unterminated final line', base, [EMPTY])\nvalid('JSON whitespace and CRLF', b' \\t' + base + b' \\r\\n', [EMPTY])\nvalid('CR is JSON whitespace', base + b'\\r', [EMPTY])\npublic = request([entry('cash', 7), entry('cash', -7), entry('bank', 3)])\npublic_result = result({'cash': 0, 'bank': 3}, 3, 3, ['cash'])\nvalid('public cancellation', public + b'\\n', [public_result])\nbig = request([entry('a', 10**12), entry('a', 10**12)])\nvalid('public aggregate exceeds movement bound', big, [result({'a': 2*10**12}, 2*10**12, 2, [])])\nvalid('negative aggregate exceeds movement bound', request([entry('a', -10**12)] * 2), [result({'a': -2*10**12}, -2*10**12, 2, [])])\nvalid('ordered independent requests', public + b'\\n' + base + b'\\n' + request([entry('cash', 4)]), [public_result, EMPTY, result({'cash': 4}, 4, 1, [])])\nvalid('lexicographic zero accounts and duplicate movements', request([entry('z', 0), entry('a_', 8), entry('a0', -3), entry('a', 2), entry('a_', -8), entry('a0', 3), entry('a', 2)]), [result({'z': 0, 'a_': 0, 'a0': 0, 'a': 4}, 4, 7, ['a0', 'a_', 'z'])])\nvalid('both individual extremes', request([entry('a', 10**12), entry('b', -10**12), entry('c', 0)]), [result({'a': 10**12, 'b': -10**12, 'c': 0}, 0, 3, ['c'])])\nvalid('account length and alphabet boundaries', request([entry('a', 1), entry('z' + '9_'*15 + '0', 2)]), [result({'a': 1, 'z' + '9_'*15 + '0': 2}, 3, 2, [])])\nvalid('decoded escaped fields and account', b'{\"entr\\u0069es\":[{\"acc\\u006funt\":\"\\u0061_9\",\"delt\\u0061\":-0}]}', [result({'a_9': 0}, 0, 1, ['a_9'])])\nvalid('reversed entry key order', b'{\"entries\":[{\"delta\":5,\"account\":\"a\"}]}', [result({'a': 5}, 5, 1, [])])\nvalid('exact byte limit including LF', base + b' '*(LIMIT-len(base)-1) + b'\\n', [EMPTY])\nvalid('exact byte limit without LF', b' '*(LIMIT-len(base)) + base, [EMPTY])\ninvalid('one byte over limit', base + b' '*(LIMIT-len(base)+1))\ninvalid('large excess after valid prefix', base + b'\\n' + b' '*(LIMIT*2))\nvalid('2000 entries maximum positive exact sum', request([entry('a', 10**12)]*2000), [result({'a': 2000*10**12}, 2000*10**12, 2000, [])])\nvalid('2000 distinct zero accounts', request([entry('a'+str(i), 0) for i in range(2000)]), [result({'a'+str(i): 0 for i in range(2000)}, 0, 2000, sorted('a'+str(i) for i in range(2000)))])\ninvalid('2001 entries', request([entry('a', 0)]*2001))\n\n# C01-C03: invalid encoding, framing, syntax and non-finite constants.\nfor label, data in [\n    ('empty line', b'\\n'),\n    ('whitespace line', b' \\t\\r\\n'),\n    ('initial empty line', b'\\n'+base),\n    ('middle empty line', base+b'\\n\\n'+base),\n    ('extra final LF', base+b'\\n\\n'),\n    ('trailing whitespace-only request', base+b'\\n \\t'),\n    ('bare CR does not separate objects', base+b'\\r'+base),\n    ('two objects on one line', base+b' '+base),\n    ('UTF-8 BOM', b'\\xef\\xbb\\xbf'+base),\n    ('invalid UTF-8 byte', base+b'\\xff'),\n    ('truncated UTF-8', base+b'\\xe2\\x82'),\n    ('overlong UTF-8', b'\\xc0\\xaf'+base),\n    ('UTF-8 surrogate encoding', b'\\xed\\xa0\\x80'+base),\n    ('Unicode line separator', base+'\\u2028'.encode('utf-8')+base),\n    ('Unicode paragraph separator', base+'\\u2029'.encode('utf-8')+base),\n    ('truncated JSON', b'{\"entries\":['),\n    ('trailing comma', b'{\"entries\":[],}'),\n    ('single quotes', b\"{'entries':[]}\"),\n    ('trailing garbage', base+b'x'),\n    ('JSON comment', base+b' // comment'),\n    ('leading zero', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"delta\":01}]}'),\n    ('plus sign number', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"delta\":+1}]}'),\n    ('unescaped control', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\\t\",\"delta\":1}]}'),\n    ('non-JSON whitespace', b'\\v'+base),\n]:\n    invalid(label, data)\nfor token in ('NaN', 'Infinity', '-Infinity'):\n    invalid('non-finite delta '+token, ('{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"delta\":'+token+'}]}').encode('ascii'))\ninvalid('non-finite nested extra field', b'{\"entries\":[],\"extra\":{\"x\":NaN}}')\n\n# C03-C06: schemas, duplicate keys at different depths and strict types.\nfor value in (None, True, 0, 'x', [], {}):\n    invalid('invalid root '+repr(value), encode(value))\ninvalid('extra root field', encode({'entries': [], 'extra': 0}))\nfor value in (None, True, 0, 'x', {}):\n    invalid('invalid entries type '+repr(value), encode({'entries': value}))\nfor value in (None, True, 0, 'x', [], {}, {'account': 'a'}, {'delta': 1}, {'account': 'a', 'delta': 1, 'extra': 0}):\n    invalid('invalid entry shape '+repr(value), request([value]))\nfor label, data in [\n    ('duplicate root key', b'{\"entries\":[],\"entries\":[]}'),\n    ('escaped duplicate root key', b'{\"entries\":[],\"entr\\u0069es\":[]}'),\n    ('duplicate account key', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"account\":\"b\",\"delta\":1}]}'),\n    ('escaped duplicate account key', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"acc\\u006funt\":\"a\",\"delta\":1}]}'),\n    ('duplicate delta key', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"delta\":1,\"delta\":2}]}'),\n    ('escaped duplicate delta key', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"delta\":1,\"delt\\u0061\":1}]}'),\n    ('duplicate key in nested object', b'{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"delta\":{\"x\":1,\"x\":2}}]}'),\n    ('duplicate key in extra nested object', b'{\"entries\":[],\"extra\":{\"x\":1,\"\\u0078\":2}}'),\n]:\n    invalid(label, data)\nfor account in ('', 'a'*33, '1a', '_a', 'A', 'a-b', 'a.b', 'a b', 'a\\n', 'a\\x00', 'é', 'aé', 'ａ', '\\ud800', None, True, 1, [], {}):\n    invalid('invalid account '+repr(account), request([entry(account, 1)]))\nfor delta in (10**12+1, -10**12-1, True, False, None, '1', [], {}):\n    invalid('invalid delta '+repr(delta), request([entry('a', delta)]))\nfor token in ('1.0', '-0.0', '1e0', '1E3', '1e9999', '9'*5000):\n    invalid('invalid numeric representation '+token[:12], ('{\"entries\":[{\"account\":\"a\",\"delta\":'+token+'}]}').encode('ascii'))\ninvalid('excessive nesting', b'{\"entries\":'+b'['*1500+b'0'+b']'*1500+b'}')\n\n# C10: reject every invalid fixture following valid requests, preventing partial\n# output. Additional placements test invalid-first and invalid-middle batches.\ninvalid('invalid first followed by valid', b'{}\\n'+public+b'\\n')\ninvalid('invalid middle between valid', public+b'\\n{}\\n'+base+b'\\n')\ninvalid('late invalid encoding', public+b'\\n'+base+b'\\n\\xff')\nvalid('many independent zero requests', b'\\n'.join([base]*100)+b'\\n', [EMPTY]*100)\n\n\nclass Battery(unittest.TestCase):\n    def cli(self, data):\n        # -I does not add the delivery directory to sys.path. run_path loads the\n        # sealed local program by absolute filename, including its CLI guard.\n        return subprocess.run(\n            [sys.executable, '-I', '-B', '-c',\n             'import runpy; runpy.run_path('+repr(str(PROGRAM))+', run_name=\"__main__\")'],\n            input=data, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n            timeout=8, check=False,\n        )\n\n    def check_invalid(self, completed):\n        need(completed.returncode == 2, 'exit')\n        need(completed.stdout == b'', 'stdout')\n        need(completed.stderr == ERROR, 'stderr')\n\n    def check_valid(self, completed, expected):\n        need(completed.returncode == 0, 'exit')\n        need(completed.stderr == b'', 'stderr')\n        if not expected:\n            need(completed.stdout == b'', 'stdout')\n            return\n        need(completed.stdout.endswith(b'\\n'), 'newline')\n        lines = completed.stdout[:-1].split(b'\\n')\n        need(len(lines) == len(expected), 'lines')\n        for line, wanted in zip(lines, expected):\n            try:\n                actual = json.loads(line.decode('utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique, parse_constant=finite)\n            except (ValueError, UnicodeError, RecursionError):\n                raise AssertionError('json') from None\n            need(type(actual) is dict and set(actual) == {'balances', 'total', 'count', 'zero_accounts'}, 'shape')\n            need(type(actual['balances']) is dict, 'shape')\n            need(all(type(k) is str and type(v) is int for k, v in actual['balances'].items()), 'types')\n            need(type(actual['total']) is int and type(actual['count']) is int, 'types')\n            need(type(actual['zero_accounts']) is list and all(type(a) is str for a in actual['zero_accounts']), 'types')\n            need(actual == wanted, 'value')\n\n\ndef install_case(index, label, data, expected):\n    def test(self):\n        completed = self.cli(data)\n        if expected is None:\n            self.check_invalid(completed)\n            # Prefix both a nonempty valid request and an empty valid request.\n            # Even formerly valid output must be absent after a later error.\n            self.check_invalid(self.cli(public+b'\\n'+base+b'\\n'+data))\n        else:\n            self.check_valid(completed, expected)\n    test.__doc__ = label\n    setattr(Battery, 'test_%03d' % index, test)\n\n\nfor case_index, case in enumerate(CASES, 1):\n    install_case(case_index, *case)\n\n\nclass ShortInput:\n    \"\"\"Binary stdin fixture that returns short reads instead of full requests.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.offset = 0\n        self.calls = []\n\n    def read(self, size):\n        need(type(size) is int and size > 0, 'read')\n        self.calls.append(size)\n        chunk = self.data[self.offset:self.offset+min(size, 997)]\n        self.offset += len(chunk)\n        return chunk\n\n\nclass Streams:\n    def __init__(self, buffer):\n        self.buffer = buffer\n\n\ndef short_read_case(self):\n    # Loading is absolute and does not invoke the guarded CLI. Only after loading\n    # do we prohibit external file access while main handles controlled streams.\n    namespace = runpy.run_path(str(PROGRAM), run_name='ledger_fold_test_module')\n    need(callable(namespace.get('main')), 'main')\n    fixtures = [\n        (base+b' '*(LIMIT-len(base)), 0, [EMPTY]),\n        (base+b' '*(LIMIT-len(base)+1), 2, None),\n        (public+b'\\n{}\\n', 2, None),\n    ]\n    for data, exit_code, expected in fixtures:\n        source = ShortInput(data)\n        out = io.BytesIO()\n        err = io.BytesIO()\n        with mock.patch.object(sys, 'stdin', Streams(source)), mock.patch.object(sys, 'stdout', Streams(out)), mock.patch.object(sys, 'stderr', Streams(err)), mock.patch('builtins.open', side_effect=AssertionError('file')), mock.patch('io.open', side_effect=AssertionError('file')):\n            code = namespace['main']()\n        completed = subprocess.CompletedProcess([], code, out.getvalue(), err.getvalue())\n        if exit_code == 2:\n            self.check_invalid(completed)\n        else:\n            self.check_valid(completed, expected)\n        need(source.offset <= LIMIT+1, 'bound')\n        need(all(size <= LIMIT+1 for size in source.calls), 'bound')\n\n\nshort_read_case.__doc__ = 'bounded short reads and main stream-only behavior'\nsetattr(Battery, 'test_%03d' % (len(CASES)+1), short_read_case)\n\n\ndef source_review_case(self):\n    # Narrow source-level check complements behavior; this is not a security\n    # proof. It examines only the supplied sealed implementation's dependency\n    # surface and obvious file/network/process entry points.\n    tree = ast.parse(PROGRAM.read_bytes(), filename=str(PROGRAM))\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Import):\n            need(all(alias.name in {'json', 're', 'sys'} for alias in node.names), 'imports')\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.ImportFrom):\n            need(node.level == 0 and node.module in {'json', 're', 'sys'}, 'imports')\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.Call):\n            if isinstance(node.func, ast.Name):\n                need(node.func.id not in {'open', 'exec', 'eval', '__import__'}, 'io')\n            elif isinstance(node.func, ast.Attribute):\n                need(node.func.attr not in {'open', 'read_text', 'read_bytes', 'write_text', 'write_bytes', 'connect', 'urlopen', 'system', 'popen'}, 'io')\n\n\nsource_review_case.__doc__ = 'limited dependency and external-operation source review'\nsetattr(Battery, 'test_%03d' % (len(CASES)+2), source_review_case)\n\n\nclass CompactResult(unittest.TestResult):\n    \"\"\"Complete case disposition summary without captured program payloads.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.issues = []\n\n    def record(self, test, code):\n        self.issues.append([int(test._testMethodName.rsplit('_', 1)[1]), code])\n\n    def addFailure(self, test, err):\n        super().addFailure(test, err)\n        # All explicit assertion codes are small, fixed strings.\n        code = err[1].args[0] if err[1].args else 'assert'\n        self.record(test, code if code in {'exit', 'stdout', 'stderr', 'newline', 'lines', 'json', 'shape', 'types', 'value', 'read', 'main', 'file', 'bound', 'imports', 'io'} else 'assert')\n\n    def addError(self, test, err):\n        super().addError(test, err)\n        self.record(test, 'error')\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    suite = unittest.defaultTestLoader.loadTestsFromTestCase(Battery)\n    report = CompactResult()\n    suite.run(report)\n    print(json.dumps({'schema': 1, 'tests': report.testsRun, 'failures': len(report.failures), 'errors': len(report.errors), 'issues': report.issues}, separators=(',', ':')))\n    sys.exit(0 if report.wasSuccessful() else 1)\n"}, "documents": {"BATTERY.md": "# Batería separada LedgerFold\n\nSe entrega únicamente test_ledger_fold.py como archivo nuevo. Los fixtures están integrados en él; no se modifican programa, README, documentos anteriores, fixtures originales ni configuración. La instrucción actual declara sellados programa y README. No se inventa un recibo de sello ni una ejecución.\n\nInvocación fija: /opt/specorganon/venv/bin/python -I -B /input/delivery/test_ledger_fold.py. La batería usa unittest y otras bibliotecas estándar. Cada subprocess carga /input/delivery/ledger_fold.py mediante runpy.run_path por ruta absoluta y ejecuta su guarda CLI con streams binarios reales. No necesita sys.path, instalación externa, red ni archivos temporales. Los tests adicionales cargan el mismo archivo absolutamente para comprobar main con lecturas cortas. Las lecturas de fuente corresponden a la batería, no al programa durante su procesamiento.\n\nCobertura vinculada a los criterios originales: C01 incluye entrada vacía, límites exactos con y sin LF, exceso de un byte, exceso amplio y UTF-8 inválido; C02 y A01–A02 incluyen LF, CRLF, última línea sin terminador, líneas vacías, espacios, BOM y separadores Unicode. C03 incluye sintaxis, contenido adicional, constantes no finitas y duplicados literales o equivalentes tras escapes en diferentes profundidades. C04 incluye formas de raíz, entries y elementos, campos ausentes/extra y 2000/2001 movimientos. C05 incluye tipos, alfabeto, escapes y longitudes 1/32/33. C06 incluye extremos, exceso de una unidad, bool, float, exponentes, tipos prohibidos y números largos. C07–C09 incluyen ejemplos públicos, cancelación, ceros, duplicados, orden lexicográfico, cuentas independientes, 2000 cuentas distintas y sumas exactas superiores al límite individual. La salida se comprueba con claves exactas, tipos enteros estrictos, JSON sin duplicados ni constantes y un LF por resultado.\n\nC10 se comprueba para cada fixture inválido tanto solo como después de dos peticiones válidas, además de posiciones iniciales e intermedias y errores tardíos de codificación. Se exige exit 2, stdout vacío y stderr exacto; para entradas válidas se exige exit 0 y stderr vacío. Las lecturas cortas comprueban el límite de lectura de main y bloquean open durante ese procesamiento. C11 recibe además una revisión AST limitada de la superficie de dependencias y operaciones evidentes del programa sellado. Estas comprobaciones no demuestran ausencia universal de efectos externos, seguridad, rendimiento ni tolerancia a fallos de sistema.\n\nC12 conserva los archivos sellados y aporta la batería separada con el nombre fijado. La evaluación documental de README y la auditoría de cronología no se convierten en resultados funcionales. El README suministrado incluye en su segunda sección de ejemplos un comando fuera de rango antes del comando válido, y conserva declaraciones de etapa anteriores sobre ausencia de batería y sello. No se corrige aquí; cualquier reparación corresponde al presupuesto posterior compartido.\n\nEl reporte previsto es un único objeto JSON compacto por stdout, sin traceback por stderr. tests cuenta todos los casos; failures y errors cuentan sus disposiciones; issues registra todos los casos fallidos o con error mediante su índice y una categoría. Los índices siguen el orden de CASES, seguido de lecturas cortas y revisión AST. Un índice ausente de issues terminó satisfactoriamente en esa ejecución. error identifica una excepción inesperada o timeout; las otras categorías identifican la primera comprobación fallida del caso. Es un resumen de disposiciones, no un registro de payloads o trazas. No se recorta ningún listado de issues. El host conserva la autoridad para generar recibos y vincular medidas a bytes concretos.\n\nNo se ha ejecutado esta batería en este turno. No hay resultado medido, aprobación final, F independiente, D/G, H ni afirmación de superioridad.\n"}}}
